Small-World properties resources:
1)Clustering Coeff:  https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/clustering-coefficient-graph-theory/
!!!! Clustering Coeff as mentioned in the article for the local computation must be seen as:
piG(v) = 1 when the neoghbours are connected to each other 
piG(v) = 0 when no neighbour is connected to another 

Thus piG(v) measures the number of edges that connect the neighbours of the v


!!!! When refering to the triplets in a triangle we must see that:
1) triplets can be centered around a node - from which 2 edges are drawn to
2) there are opened and closed triplets

!!!! In a triangle we have 3 possible centers for our triplets, thus 3 triplets are considered to belong to the triangle

